  ('53849910476', 'Rho Ophiuchi Composite (Chandra/Webb composite)', 'This is a composite image from NASA’s Chandra X-ray Observatory and the James Webb Space Telescope. Pictured is Rho Ophiuchi, at a distance of about 390 light-years from Earth. Rho Ophiuchi is a cloud', '2023-07-12T00:00:00', 7, 'https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/53849910476_01c356b55b_o.jpg'),
  ('53849921521', 'Orion Nebula (Chandra/Webb composite)', 'This is a composite image from NASA’s Chandra X-ray Observatory and the James Webb Space Telescope. Pictured is the Orion Nebula, a giant cloud where stars are forming. Still located in the Milky Way ', '2007-10-03T00:00:00', 6, 'https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/53849921521_930e9c4fb7_o.jpg'),
  ('53850188868', 'NGC 3627 (Chandra/Webb/Hubble composite)', 'This is a composite image from NASA’s Chandra X-ray Observatory, the Hubble Space Telescope, and the James Webb Space Telescope. Pictured is galaxy NGC 3627, located 36 million light-years away. Like ', '2023-01-12T11:46:15', 4, 'https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/53850188868_412782ced8_o.jpg'),
  ('53850956067', 'Interacting Galaxies Arp 142 (NIRCam only)', 'Penguins make excellent parents, even in space. 🐧 This new Webb image shows two galaxies: a Penguin (NGC 2936) guarding an Egg (NGC 2937). Webb’s observations reveal the two are in a cosmic hug, joine', '2024-07-12T10:07:41', 11, 'https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/53850956067_b3cafe31e8_o.png'),
  ('53851864526', 'Interacting Galaxies Arp 142 (MIRI only)', 'Webb’s mid-infrared view of interacting galaxies Arp 142 seems to sing in primary colors. The background of space is like a yawning darkness speckled with bright, multi-colored beads. This image was t', '2024-07-12T10:17:34', 7, 'https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/53851864526_81b2684f52_o.png'),
  ('53852202289', 'Vivid Portrait of Interacting Galaxies Marks Webb''s Second Anniversary (NIRCam and MIRI)', 'Penguins make excellent parents, even in space. 🐧 This new Webb image shows two galaxies: a Penguin (NGC 2936) guarding an Egg (NGC 2937). Webb’s observations reveal the two are in a cosmic hug, joine', '2024-07-12T10:04:06', 4, 'https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/53852202289_48fd81ca74_o.png'),
  ('53852285870', 'Arp 142 (Full Field/NIRCam only)', 'Penguins make excellent parents, even in space. 🐧 This new Webb image shows two galaxies: a Penguin (NGC 2936) guarding an Egg (NGC 2937). Webb’s observations reveal the two are in a cosmic hug, joine', '2024-07-12T10:08:11', 7, 'https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/53852285870_01497c017d_o.png'),
  ('53852308510', 'Interacting Galaxies Arp 142 (Hubble and Webb Image)', 'Two penguins, two eggs — two very different color schemes! The Hubble Space Telescope captured visible light when observing Arp 142, nicknamed the Penguin and the Egg, in 2013. At right is the James W', '2024-07-12T10:21:23', 4, 'https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/53852308510_c27ce266f7_o.png'),
  ('53858577846', 'Hot Gas Giant Exoplanet WASP-39 b Transit Light Curve (NIRSpec)', 'A light curve from NASA’s James Webb Space Telescope’s NIRSpec (Near-Infrared Spectrograph) shows the change in brightness from the WASP-39 star system over time as the planet transited the star. This', '2024-07-15T12:08:20', 3, 'https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/53858577846_17a5be0485_o.png'),
  ('53858833523', 'NASA''s Webb Investigates Eternal Sunrises, Sunsets on Distant World (Artist Concept)', 'WASP-39 b is a tidally locked planet: One side is in eternal day, the other in eternal night. By observing the day/night boundary, Webb has confirmed — with extraordinary precision — the differences i', '2024-07-15T12:12:58', 3, 'https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/53858833523_2c7beceea6_o.png'),
  ('53858945264', 'Hot Gas Giant Exoplanet WASP-39 b Transmission Spectrum (NIRSpec)', 'This transmission spectrum, captured using Webb’s NIRSpec (Near-Infrared Spectrograph) PRISM bright object-time series mode, shows the amounts of near-infrared starlight blocked by the atmosphere of h', '2024-07-15T12:08:28', 3, 'https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/53858945264_4bd810cbb0_o.png'),
  ('53875246097', 'Orion Nebula for Chandra''s 25th Anniversary (Chandra/Webb composite)', 'One of the closest regions of star formation to Earth, newly-formed stars in the Orion Nebula are detected by Chandra. X-rays from Chandra (magenta) and infrared from Webb (red, green, and blue). Read', '2024-07-23T11:34:38', 6, 'https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/53875246097_65f7cfcfff_o.jpg'),
  ('53876176351', 'Pillars of Creation (M16) for Chandra''s 25th Anniversary (Chandra/Webb composite)', 'This region of star formation contains the Pillars of Creation, which was made famous by the Hubble Space Telescope. Chandra detects X-rays from young stars in the region, including one embedded in a ', '2024-07-23T11:45:49', 7, 'https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/53876176351_9cbdfa7df1_o.jpg'),
  ('53876287721', 'SN 1987A for Chandra''s 25th Anniversary (Chandra/Webb/Hubble composite)', 'The supernova explosion that created this object was first observed on Earth in February 1987. Chandra sees X-rays produced by debris from the explosion. X-rays from Chandra (purple); optical and infr', '2024-07-23T12:31:19', 7, 'https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/53876287721_c3fd5f2edf_o.jpg'),
  ('53876457898', 'WR 124 for Chandra''s 25th Anniversary (Chandra/Webb/Herschel/Spitzer/WISE composite)', 'WR 124 is a rare type of Wolf-Rayet star, a bright, massive star experiencing a short-lived phase in its evolution. A dense wind from the star may prevent the detection with Chandra of a neutron star ', '2024-07-23T12:04:46', 7, 'https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/53876457898_0662d90a15_o.jpg'),
  ('53876484333', 'Orion Nebula for Chandra''s 25th Anniversary (Chandra/Webb composite)', 'The Cassiopeia A supernova remnant has been observed for more than 2 million seconds since the start of the Chandra mission in 1999. X-rays from Chandra (blue); infrared from Webb (orange, white, and ', '2024-07-23T12:14:41', 7, 'https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/53876484333_958b3c2c84_o.jpg'),
  ('53876605450', 'NGC 7469 for Chandra''s 25th Anniversary (Chandra/Webb/Hubble composite)', 'NGC 7469 is a spiral galaxy, seen face on, that contains a growing supermassive black hole. Chandra shows hot gas near the black hole. X-rays from Chandra (purple); optical/IR from Hubble (red, green,', '2024-07-23T11:52:44', 7, 'https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/53876605450_542a710aea_o.jpg'),
  ('53876623114', 'NGC 3324 for Chandra''s 25th Anniversary (Chandra/Webb composite)', 'Astronomers nicknamed this region of star formation the “Cosmic Cliffs,” which is found in the nearby Carina Nebula. X-rays from young stars in two clusters are detected by Chandra. X-rays from Chandr', '2024-07-23T12:27:16', 7, 'https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/53876623114_a7f20e1dbb_o.jpg'),
  ('53876628304', 'NGC 1365 for Chandra''s 25th Anniversary (Chandra/Webb composite)', 'This spiral galaxy contains a supermassive black hole and stars rapidly forming in its center. Chandra sees X-rays from gas near the massive black hole and from smaller black holes or neutron stars pu', '2024-07-23T12:29:19', 4, 'https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/53876628304_21c35e26f3_o.jpg'),
  ('53878708659', 'NASA''s Webb Images Cold Exoplanet 12 Light-Years Away', 'NEW: Webb has snapped a shot of the coldest, most Jupiter-like exoplanet to be imaged so far. The planet, called Epsilon Indi Ab, lies about 12 light-years away from Earth. To make the discovery, Webb', '2024-07-24T11:05:21', 3, 'https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/53878708659_8390a20ebf_o.png'),
  ('53879651047', 'Webb Model by Josef Maroušek', 'This Webb model was submitted by 9th grader Josef Maroušek of the Czech Republic. Find the model templates here: <a href="https://jwst.nasa.gov/content/features/educational/paperModel/paperModel.html"', '2024-07-25T11:55:31', 11, 'https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/53879651047_e7134be13c_o.jpg'),
  ('53880745638', 'Webb Model by Shanzay Umair Khan', 'This Webb model was submitted by 4th grader Shanzay Umair Khan from Pakistan. She says, &quot;For my Science exhibition project, I chose to create a model of the James Webb telescope as I believe it i', '2024-05-11T16:28:33', 11, 'https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/53880745638_61cf1a02d0_o.jpg'),
  ('53880904940', 'Webb Model by Aivin Siby Nilakkapallil , Ronell Biju Chacko, Aaron Francis Thomas and Abel Jacob', 'This Webb model was submitted by Aivin Siby Nilakkapallil , Ronell Biju Chacko, Aaron Francis Thomas and Abel Jacob. Find the model templates here: <a href="https://jwst.nasa.gov/content/features/educ', '2024-07-25T11:23:31', 11, 'https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/53880904940_0acaf05496_o.jpg'),
  ('53912178488', 'The hidden intricacies of Messier 106', 'Won’t you be our cosmic neighbor, M106? This galaxy, with a very active black hole, is one of the brightest and nearest spiral galaxies to ours. Its central region is lit up by its black hole actively', '2024-08-09T10:00:00', 4, 'https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/53912178488_3ab9e86872_o.jpg');
INSERT INTO OBSERVATIONS (OBSERVATION_ID, TITLE, DESCRIPTION, OBSERVED_AT, CATEGORY_ID, IMAGE_URL) VALUES
  ('53949426179', 'Webb Finds Early Galaxies Weren''t Too Big for Their Britches After All', 'Did Webb’s look at early galaxies really break cosmology? (Spoiler alert: nope!) The issue? How to explain unexpectedly bright early galaxies. If these galaxies were bright because rapid star formatio', '2024-08-26T10:05:09', 1, 'https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/53949426179_1e3cd55d2b_o.png'),
  ('53951942710', 'Peeking into Perseus (NGC 1333)', 'A stellar view! NGC 1333 is a nearby star-forming region. Webb’s sharp infrared vision lets us peer through the dusty veil to reveal newborn stars, brown dwarfs, and planetary mass objects. Many of th', '2024-08-27T09:33:06', 7, 'https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/53951942710_9389759151_o.png'),
  ('53969828422', 'Question Mark Galaxy - Hubble and Webb', 'NASA’s Hubble Space Telescope has also observed the galaxy cluster MACS-J0417.5-1154, but the dusty red galaxy that appears multiple times to form a question mark shape is much more prominent in the W', '2024-09-04T10:08:27', 5, 'https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/53969828422_c9e29c8e3f_o.png'),
  ('53970855226', 'MACS J0417.5-1154 Wide Field (plus Question Mark Galaxy) (NIRCam)', 'A cosmic question mark appears amid a powerful gravitational lens in the James Webb Space Telescope’s wide-field view of the galaxy cluster MACS-J0417.5-1154. Gravitational lensing occurs when somethi', '2024-09-04T11:14:34', 5, 'https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/53970855226_7babeecbff_o.png'),
  ('53971042139', 'NASA''s Webb Reveals Distorted Galaxy Forming Cosmic Question Mark (NIRCam)', '? 🤔 Thanks to a cosmic magnifying glass effect, the gravity of a massive galaxy cluster is warping two distant interacting galaxies (a face-on spiral and a dusty red galaxy) behind it, making them app', '2024-09-04T10:08:18', 5, 'https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/53971042139_24662be98e_o.png'),
  ('53987646431', '#JWSTArt and #UnfoldTheUniverse art - by Jacob Whitehead', 'An addition to our #UnfoldTheUniverse social media campaign by Jacob Whitehead. If you create art inspired by the James Webb Space Telescope, share it with us! For terms and more information, please v', '2024-09-11T10:29:06', 9, 'https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/53987646431_81d95903d5_o.png'),
  ('53987719486', '#UnfoldTheUniverse art - by  Julia Curylo', 'An addition to our #UnfoldTheUniverse social media campaign by Julia Curylo. Julia says, &quot;The two paintings I am sending are dedicated to the Webb Telescope. They feature a motif inspired by its ', '2023-03-23T13:28:11', 11, 'https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/53987719486_3559059f56_o.jpg'),
  ('53987739496', '#UnfoldTheUniverse art - by Patricia Backer', 'An addition to our #UnfoldTheUniverse social media campaign by Patricia Backer. Patricia says, &quot;This is a quilt I designed using a fabric panel of the Carina Nebula taken by the JWST.&quot; If yo', '2024-09-11T11:10:36', 11, 'https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/53987739496_a48aa4c091_o.jpg'),
